  universityChannels: 'Students with an IB Diploma or Cambridge/Pearson Edexcel A-Levels apply to Danish universities through optagelse.dk, the national coordinated admission system used by every Danish higher-education institution. The IB Diploma is directly recognised as equivalent to a Danish upper-secondary leaving certificate (minimum 24 points, individual programme subject requirements apply); Cambridge and Edexcel A-Levels are assessed on a comparable basis, with grades converted to the Danish 7-point scale by the Danish Agency for Higher Education. Danish higher education is free for EU/EEA citizens and permanent residents; other international students pay roughly EUR 6,000-20,000/year. Many Danish bachelor\'s programmes are taught in Danish and require documented Danish language proficiency, but Denmark also offers over 600 programmes taught fully in English — a genuine, substantial pathway for non-Danish-speaking Cambridge or IB graduates. Internationally, Cambridge A-Levels are accepted by universities in 160+ countries via UCAS (UK) or direct application; the IB Diploma is recognised globally. Smartious provides personalised university guidance across Danish (optagelse.dk), UK (UCAS), and US (Common Application) destinations.',
