  britishCurriculumSuits: 'Denmark families targeting the Cambridge IGCSE + A-Level pathway. Best fit for: (1) families whose children are ageing out of Denmark\'s limited local international-school options (particularly relevant in Aarhus, Odense, Aalborg, Esbjerg, and Billund), (2) families relocating from the UK maintaining British curriculum trajectory to UCAS, (3) corporate and technical rotational families needing curriculum portability, (4) families targeting Danish universities via the optagelse.dk pathway.',
  britishCurriculumDelivery: 'Live online classes scheduled to land within the Danish school day given the 1-2 hour CET/CEST-EAT offset, small groups 4-6 students. Cambridge examinations through British Council Copenhagen.',
  ibDiplomaSuits: 'Denmark families targeting the IB Diploma\'s breadth — a natural continuation for children completing the Middle Years Programme at Aarhus International School or a similar MYP school, or for families targeting Danish, US, or European universities with holistic applications.',
  ibDiplomaDelivery: 'Live online IB DP classes across all six subject groups plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay supervision.',
  americanCurriculumSuits: 'Denmark families targeting US universities via Common Application — corporate families connected to Novo Nordisk, Maersk, LEGO, and Denmark\'s broader multinational employer base.',
  americanCurriculumDelivery: 'American Curriculum with AP courses Grades 9-12, SAT/ACT preparation, Common App essay coaching.',
  founderBioCountrySpecific: 'Alfred Ouko founded Smartious in 2019 to make international qualifications (Cambridge, IB, American) accessible to families across emerging markets and international corporate rotational communities at online-delivery fees. Denmark families join students in 20 other countries — from Copenhagen\'s Nordhavn to Nairobi\'s own Diamond Plaza HQ, Madrid\'s La Moraleja to Dubai\'s Downtown.',
  founderUniversitySpecialism: 'Alfred holds a BEd in Mathematics and Physics — Smartious\'s Cambridge A-Level and IB Diploma STEM subjects are led personally when needed. Head of Academics supervises curriculum delivery and university placement strategy per family, including the optagelse.dk pathway for Danish university destinations.',

  competitorsIntro: 'Denmark has a real but comparatively compact international school landscape concentrated in Copenhagen, with thinner coverage in Aarhus, Odense, Aalborg, Esbjerg, and Billund. Fees for established schools typically run DKK 25,000-78,000/year — genuinely lower than London, Geneva, or many of the other markets Smartious serves. Denmark\'s one clear dedicated online home-education competitor currently serves only ages 4-15, leaving no live online Cambridge or A-Level continuation option in the Danish market before Smartious.',
